== next (exit 0)
would run: a batch's suite still running (target/suite.lock/testing): wait for it and handle it (drive_settle) first
would run: target/fast/nikaia run scripts/agent.nika -- T/b1.md --dir T
would run: git add T/b1.md.report.md T/b1.md.run.json T/cost.txt docs/tokenspeed.md
would run: git commit -m 'briefs: b1 report' -- T/b1.md.report.md T/b1.md.run.json T/cost.txt docs/tokenspeed.md
would run: append T/b1.md to T/unpushed.txt (no suite until the batch ends)
DRY-RUN NEXT b1
== batch done (exit 0)
would run: a suite still running (target/suite.lock/testing): wait for it first (SUITE <sha8> waiting)
would run: git fetch origin develop; git rev-list --count origin/develop..HEAD (0: nothing to test)
would run: git log --format= --name-only origin/develop..HEAD: all documentation by scripts/ci-changes.sh's rule, push HEAD without the suite (SUITE <sha8> docs-only, pushed without the suite), empty T/unpushed.txt
would run: mkdir target/suite.lock (wait while its owner's pid lives)
would run: after the lock and before each suite: git fetch origin develop; git rev-list --count origin/develop..HEAD (0: SUITE nothing new after the lock, empty T/unpushed.txt, rm -rf target/suite.lock)
would run: git push --force origin <sha>:refs/heads/ci/<last part of DIR> (the whole CI workflow runs on that push); in the background: target/fast/nikaia run scripts/drive.nika -- --ci-wait <sha> T/suite.log target/suite.lock/exit-<sha> (gh api every 30 s; Gate: green, or Gate: red <failed jobs> with their log tails); the architect starts at once
would run: before the next batch's first builder (or a bump, or the end): wait for it; green: git push origin <sha>:develop, drop the tested briefs from T/unpushed.txt, rm -rf target/suite.lock
would run: red: write T/qa-input.txt, mkdir -p T/qa, copy docs/briefs/qa-task.md to T/qa/qa-task.md (its report path made T/qa/qa-task.md.report.md), rm -f T/qa/qa-task.md.report.md, target/fast/nikaia run scripts/agent.nika -- T/qa/qa-task.md --dir T, commit T/qa/qa-task.md with its report and run files, the suite again and waited for (at most 2 QA rounds)
would run: write T/architect-input.txt: BATCH DONE
would run: rm -f T/architect-task.md.report.md
would run: target/fast/nikaia run scripts/agent.nika -- T/architect-task.md --dir T
would run: git add T/cost.txt docs/tokenspeed.md
would run: git commit -m 'briefs: architect-task report' -- T/cost.txt docs/tokenspeed.md
would run: append T/architect-task.md to T/unpushed.txt (tested with the next batch)
DRY-RUN ARCHITECT BATCH DONE
